#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "546085f7-b447-560f-8e03-5f9f83d6f2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282406} {:answer/id #uuid "74f33be1-f6b9-527c-9c36-b38596ce0f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282688} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6ac22c-45ee-5e02-aa23-fa2d93a62a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282915} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8a9385-1ddd-50d1-9fa6-1227b2a8f619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282916} {:answer/id #uuid "91107c67-4b51-563a-9b9f-7ec21682f202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6ac22c-45ee-5e02-aa23-fa2d93a62a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282915} :answer-field/id #uuid "db0740db-ef2c-573e-a13f-6da541dd04e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f247252-c196-59cb-b56b-5c53685b26d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-170668" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,x={t}^{2},$ and $y=t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot 2t+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021a846a-8825-55bf-a7b3-1dc5c5c5ff19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281709} {:answer/id #uuid "49b2d0a3-8640-5928-a7d2-f8a14102a68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282314} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a1e1c7-9e8a-5f17-9500-4d7507d44b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283715} {:answer/id #uuid "efd819c9-60d2-5826-9266-3dba4a49aaec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283779} {:answer/id #uuid "f5de75cd-c44e-5baf-9f07-d98f3333edab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49b2d0a3-8640-5928-a7d2-f8a14102a68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282314} :answer-field/id #uuid "d658fcd0-7d37-5a87-a5b6-42706ffef583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdba7da9-8893-51f6-a38d-eccc847b176c" :question/math-academy-id "q-170670" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ and $y={x}^{2}+1,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)}{{x}^{2}+1}=2x, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ed13b87-51ab-547d-a9ed-960eda7db24e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5774d438-8549-5c81-9843-45d115052cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358513} {:answer/id #uuid "63dc5334-1342-5ac0-8adc-34168c5ef7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(s+2){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358624} {:answer/id #uuid "97245f20-2357-5a46-9419-5584f26e4952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359074} {:answer/id #uuid "bc07b503-6a18-5c74-b532-0d144efdccab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s(s+2){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359386} {:answer/id #uuid "c201f1bf-9034-567f-9849-2029c4f2719a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{2}{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97245f20-2357-5a46-9419-5584f26e4952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359074} :answer-field/id #uuid "1991f021-d4bd-5ba5-9a63-d5673c4d3078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40900f6f-b4af-5c59-b5c2-386989d530fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95080" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)={e}^{x+2y},x={s}^{2},$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{x+2y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{e}^{x+2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & ={e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}\\cdot 2s+2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2s{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}+2{e}^{{s}^{2}+2s} \\\\  & =2(s+1){e}^{{s}^{2}+2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134e5ec5-1833-5763-a152-935445c16e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357915} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfec4cb-8120-5f44-9db6-9fe99f5be666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357993} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd7195e-4163-5d9b-ab1f-f50c56f9bda4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358725} {:answer/id #uuid "a03e6cf2-e199-53c6-82f6-4585f233d777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359150} {:answer/id #uuid "e14a9608-4f8c-580c-b913-718d374bebe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{1+x{e}^{-x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a03e6cf2-e199-53c6-82f6-4585f233d777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359150} :answer-field/id #uuid "69e0f45c-fd3c-57d2-96aa-73479d2efe99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d95d5a8a-ad5f-52dc-beb9-600c878518d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95088" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+y}$ and $y={e}^{-x},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}\\cdot (-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}+\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1+{e}^{-x}}{(x+{e}^{-x})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1457941c-efa8-556f-9df7-3c5ae7b44ced" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Multivariable Function With One Independent Variable in the Special Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f7371e6-fa62-5258-b977-84ee4e88782e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358438} {:answer/id #uuid "67710e58-3007-513b-8494-0c76521975c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358654} {:answer/id #uuid "80e19a52-081f-5b37-8339-414407ee7d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358876} {:answer/id #uuid "901dd65d-6c65-58cd-87bb-517a683c4833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359008} {:answer/id #uuid "96f6c6ee-cd4d-5972-a765-20abbc025c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96f6c6ee-cd4d-5972-a765-20abbc025c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d31946ed-c60d-5761-b68f-54a6782e1347" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e7ed0c3-433c-5b76-94b3-8ee539ba166f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95114" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $y={x}^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{4})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
